Small teams should avoid hardcoding secrets and use provider-specific CI secrets (e.g., GitHub Actions Secrets, GitLab CI Variables). Keep secrets encrypted at rest and never in repo history. For shared environments, use a vault like HashiCorp Vault or AWS Secrets Manager with short-lived credentials.  

Run visual regression tests on critical UI changes to catch unintended side effects from secret injection (e.g., debug logs leaking tokens). Use CI job isolation and audit logs to track access. Start simple—just secrets in the CI platform—and scale as needed.

