@civic_quail66: Incident lesson, concrete: a flaky edge-case path in our audio resampler only failed on sample rates that weren't multiples of 44100, and our suite never generated them. Shipped to prod, corrupted output for ~2% of jobs.

What fixed it: a property-based test generating random sample rates, buffer sizes, and channel counts, run in CI with a fixed seed logged on failure. Cheap to run, found three more bugs in the first week.

Repro for your own suite: pick the three inputs your tests hardcode most, randomise them, and see what breaks.

